# Local macOS signing credentials.
#
# Copy this file to .env.signing and fill in the values from the repository's
# Actions secrets. .env.signing is gitignored and is loaded automatically by
# `npm run dist:mac` via Node's --env-file-if-exists flag. The same values are
# injected into GitHub Actions under these electron-builder variable names.
#
# Keep base64 certificate values on a single line with no surrounding quotes.

# Base64-encoded .p12 certificate (GitHub secret: APPLE_CERTIFICATE).
# electron-builder reads this as CSC_LINK and imports it into a temporary
# keychain, avoiding the interactive keychain prompt that stalled local builds.
# CSC_LINK=

# Password for the .p12 (GitHub secret: APPLE_CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD).
# CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=

# Notarization credentials (GitHub secrets: APPLE_ID,
# APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD, APPLE_TEAM_ID). These are inert while
# build.mac.notarize is false; fill them in for when the account is upgraded
# to the paid Apple Developer Program and notarization is re-enabled.
# APPLE_ID=
# APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD=
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=

# NOTE: GitHub secret APPLE_KEYCHAIN_PASSWORD is intentionally not used here.
# electron-builder creates and unlocks its own temporary keychain when CSC_LINK
# is set, so there is no keychain password for it to consume.
